03:01.160 --> 03:05.620
Because I wasn't studying, yeah, I wasn't studying finance or anything like that.

03:05.700 --> 03:09.440
But I always had it in the back of my mind that that's what I want to do one day.

03:10.040 --> 03:12.520
That was a long time ago, more than 10 years ago.

03:12.940 --> 03:19.040
So and then as Arun said, we actually were both using MarketCypherB at the same time during

03:19.040 --> 03:20.120
the previous bull cycle.

03:20.120 --> 03:21.600
And he reached out to me.

03:22.020 --> 03:24.260
And Arun's exceptional with his risk management.

03:24.260 --> 03:27.260
So he actually taught me a lot about risk management.

03:27.260 --> 03:30.760
And yeah, we just carried on going from there.

03:31.080 --> 03:35.340
There's some interesting takeaways from that then.

03:35.760 --> 03:40.660
So Arun, you've come into trading as almost as a common man like most people do.

03:41.480 --> 03:48.040
This is a trade that is, when you get into it, it's painted as being anyone can do it.

03:48.040 --> 03:51.440
But it is one of the hardest businesses out there.

03:51.820 --> 03:57.200
And when Kirsten got into trading, the people in her life were saying, don't do this.

03:57.400 --> 03:58.100
You know what I'm saying?

03:59.980 --> 04:03.040
And it's like that with me, with the people in my life too.

04:03.120 --> 04:07.760
Anytime someone close to me says that they want to get into trading, I always tell them

04:07.760 --> 04:12.220
to, you know, wait a second, you know, think about it a little bit before you do it.

04:12.440 --> 04:17.740
And it's rare that, you know, me and my brother are both in trading.

04:18.040 --> 04:22.960
And it's rare that you have two people in the same family that get into it because it's

04:22.960 --> 04:24.640
a tough business.

04:24.640 --> 04:27.640
Yeah, it's interesting what you say that.

04:27.760 --> 04:29.480
I think, you know, you're right.

04:29.560 --> 04:34.040
Like a lot of people that see the successes or, you know, the Instagrams and all those

04:34.040 --> 04:36.660
kind of things say, oh, I'm going to do trading and I'm going to be successful.

04:37.020 --> 04:37.640
And you're right.

04:37.720 --> 04:40.880
Like similar to you, I always say, wait, hold on for a second.

04:41.720 --> 04:43.240
Do you really want to get into this?

04:43.340 --> 04:44.320
Have you got the right mindset?

04:44.440 --> 04:47.940
But, you know, one thing I would say is that, you know, throughout the journey that I've

04:47.940 --> 04:52.860
been on and Kirsten's been on as well is that I think trading is definitely probably

04:52.860 --> 04:58.200
the hardest thing you can achieve, but at the same time, it forces you to really work

04:58.200 --> 04:59.580
on self-development faster.

04:59.960 --> 05:06.280
Like a lot of people that don't trade, I feel don't work as hard on themselves maybe

05:06.280 --> 05:09.140
potentially, and you have to work on yourself to be a successful trader.

05:09.540 --> 05:10.240
It's true.

05:10.720 --> 05:11.160
Yeah.

05:11.560 --> 05:13.220
I agree 100%.

05:13.220 --> 05:19.120
I think that trading's fast-tracked my growth and I'm already getting older and I still

05:19.120 --> 05:19.880
have a lot of growing.

05:20.020 --> 05:22.440
So who knows how slow I would have been without trading.

05:22.860 --> 05:23.040
Yeah.

05:23.260 --> 05:23.660
Yeah.

05:24.600 --> 05:26.700
It's supposed to be expensive stuff, isn't it?

05:27.180 --> 05:27.580
Oh, yeah.

05:27.660 --> 05:32.860
I feel like I have, even though I'm clean shaven, I feel like internally I have like the beard

05:32.860 --> 05:35.520
of a 10,000-year-old wizard doing this stuff.

05:35.840 --> 05:37.700
So, yeah.

05:37.900 --> 05:40.700
So do one of you guys want to like share your screen?

05:41.360 --> 05:43.640
And so you guys trade Forex.

05:43.640 --> 05:49.580
